IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`
IMPORT `P3-section-3`

-- P3-art-27: Article 27 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744): fundamental rights impact assessment for high-risk AI systems.
-- Lines 513-526 of the consolidated text. Paragraphs 4 and 5 were replaced by the Omnibus (the passages marked M1 at lines 525 and 526); the text as enacted is lines 1056 and 1057 of the base text. Paragraphs 1 to 3 are unchanged.
-- Article 2(13) names Articles 9 to 15 and 17 to 25, not Article 27: the gate gives Article 27 the same date and Art 2(2) tests as the others and never limits it under Art 2(13).
-- The party is the deployer (Art 3(4)); the keel decides who is one. Seams: Articles 13 and 46(1) and the data protection impact assessment (Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679, Article 27 of Directive (EU) 2016/680) are plain BOOLEAN inputs named for where they come from; PLAN.md section 4 lists none of them for this part.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE met or permitted; JUST FALSE the duty applies and is not met; NOTHING not covered (the group does not yet apply, or the paragraph's own trigger is absent: limited by its own wording).

DECLARE `Art 27 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 27(1) perform an assessment of the impact on fundamental rights prior to deploying the high-risk AI system`
    `Art 27(2) take the necessary steps to update the information`
    `Art 27(3) notify the market surveillance authority of the results of the assessment, submitting the filled-out template`
    `Art 27(4) as enacted complement the data protection impact assessment`
    `Art 27(4) as amended include cross-references to the data protection impact assessment or include relevant parts of it in the fundamental rights impact assessment`

§ `Article 27(1): who must assess the impact on fundamental rights, and what the assessment consists of`

-- src:515 | 1. Prior to deploying a high-risk AI system referred to in Article 6(2), with the exception of high-risk AI systems intended to be used in the area listed in point 2 of Annex III, deployers that are bodies governed by public law, or are private entities providing public services, and deployers of high-risk AI systems referred to in points 5 (b) and (c) of Annex III, shall perform an assessment of the impact on fundamental rights that the use of such system may produce. For that purpose, deployers shall perform an assessment consisting of:
-- src:516 | (a) a description of the deployer’s processes in which the high-risk AI system will be used in line with its intended purpose;
-- src:517 | (b) a description of the period of time within which, and the frequency with which, each high-risk AI system is intended to be used;
-- src:518 | (c) the categories of natural persons and groups likely to be affected by its use in the specific context;
-- src:519 | (d) the specific risks of harm likely to have an impact on the categories of natural persons or groups of persons identified pursuant to point (c) of this paragraph, taking into account the information given by the provider pursuant to Article 13;
-- src:520 | (e) a description of the implementation of human oversight measures, according to the instructions for use;
-- src:521 | (f) the measures to be taken in the case of the materialisation of those risks, including the arrangements for internal governance and complaint mechanisms.
@ref Art 27(1) (src:515-521)
DECLARE `Art 27(1) who and what` HAS
    `the deployer is a body governed by public law`                                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deployer is a private entity providing public services`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the high-risk AI system is referred to in points 5 (b) and (c) of Annex III`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the high-risk AI system is intended to be used in the area listed in point 2 of Annex III`                   IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:516 | (a) a description of the deployer’s processes in which the high-risk AI system will be used in line with its intended purpose;
-- src:517 | (b) a description of the period of time within which, and the frequency with which, each high-risk AI system is intended to be used;
-- src:518 | (c) the categories of natural persons and groups likely to be affected by its use in the specific context;
-- src:519 | (d) the specific risks of harm likely to have an impact on the categories of natural persons or groups of persons identified pursuant to point (c) of this paragraph, taking into account the information given by the provider pursuant to Article 13;
-- src:520 | (e) a description of the implementation of human oversight measures, according to the instructions for use;
-- src:521 | (f) the measures to be taken in the case of the materialisation of those risks, including the arrangements for internal governance and complaint mechanisms.
@ref Art 27(1) points (a) to (f) (src:516-521)
DECLARE `Art 27(1) the assessment` HAS
    `the assessment contains a description of the deployer's processes in which the high-risk AI system will be used in line with its intended purpose`                                   IS A BOOLEAN  -- (a)
    `the assessment contains a description of the period of time within which, and the frequency with which, each high-risk AI system is intended to be used`                              IS A BOOLEAN  -- (b)
    `the assessment contains the categories of natural persons and groups likely to be affected by its use in the specific context`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN  -- (c)
    `the assessment contains the specific risks of harm likely to have an impact on those categories, taking into account the information given by the provider pursuant to Article 13` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (d)
    `the assessment contains a description of the implementation of human oversight measures, according to the instructions for use`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN  -- (e)
    `the assessment contains the measures to be taken in the case of the materialisation of those risks, including the arrangements for internal governance and complaint mechanisms`      IS A BOOLEAN  -- (f)

-- The deployers caught are "deployers that are bodies governed by public law, or are private entities providing public services, and deployers of high-risk AI systems referred to in points 5 (b) and (c) of Annex III", for "a high-risk AI system referred to in Article 6(2)" (route Annex III in the `AI system` record, seam S1),
-- "with the exception of high-risk AI systems intended to be used in the area listed in point 2 of Annex III". An exception is the text's own no (JUST FALSE); a deployer that is none of the three kinds is not named (NOTHING, list not closed with "only").
-- src:515 | 1. Prior to deploying a high-risk AI system referred to in Article 6(2), with the exception of high-risk AI systems intended to be used in the area listed in point 2 of Annex III, deployers that are bodies governed by public law, or are private entities providing public services, and deployers of high-risk AI systems referred to in points 5 (b) and (c) of Annex III, shall perform an assessment of the impact on fundamental rights that the use of such system may produce. For that purpose, deployers shall perform an assessment consisting of:
-- src:516 | (a) a description of the deployer’s processes in which the high-risk AI system will be used in line with its intended purpose;
-- src:517 | (b) a description of the period of time within which, and the frequency with which, each high-risk AI system is intended to be used;
-- src:518 | (c) the categories of natural persons and groups likely to be affected by its use in the specific context;
-- src:519 | (d) the specific risks of harm likely to have an impact on the categories of natural persons or groups of persons identified pursuant to point (c) of this paragraph, taking into account the information given by the provider pursuant to Article 13;
-- src:520 | (e) a description of the implementation of human oversight measures, according to the instructions for use;
-- src:521 | (f) the measures to be taken in the case of the materialisation of those risks, including the arrangements for internal governance and complaint mechanisms.
@ref Art 27(1) (src:515-521)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the facts` IS AN `Art 27(1) who and what`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 27(1) the deployer is required to perform an assessment of the impact on fundamental rights` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT (`the AI system`'s `route` EQUALS `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Prior to deploying a high-risk AI system referred to in Article 6(2)"
        ELSE IF `the facts`'s `the high-risk AI system is intended to be used in the area listed in point 2 of Annex III`
             THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "with the exception of high-risk AI systems intended to be used in the area listed in point 2 of Annex III"
             ELSE IF       `the facts`'s `the deployer is a body governed by public law`
                        OR `the facts`'s `the deployer is a private entity providing public services`
                        OR `the facts`'s `the high-risk AI system is referred to in points 5 (b) and (c) of Annex III`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph names bodies governed by public law, private entities providing public services and deployers of systems in points 5 (b) and (c) of Annex III, and does not close the list with "only"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 27, "", 0)

-- src:515 | 1. Prior to deploying a high-risk AI system referred to in Article 6(2), with the exception of high-risk AI systems intended to be used in the area listed in point 2 of Annex III, deployers that are bodies governed by public law, or are private entities providing public services, and deployers of high-risk AI systems referred to in points 5 (b) and (c) of Annex III, shall perform an assessment of the impact on fundamental rights that the use of such system may produce. For that purpose, deployers shall perform an assessment consisting of:
-- src:516 | (a) a description of the deployer’s processes in which the high-risk AI system will be used in line with its intended purpose;
-- src:517 | (b) a description of the period of time within which, and the frequency with which, each high-risk AI system is intended to be used;
-- src:518 | (c) the categories of natural persons and groups likely to be affected by its use in the specific context;
-- src:519 | (d) the specific risks of harm likely to have an impact on the categories of natural persons or groups of persons identified pursuant to point (c) of this paragraph, taking into account the information given by the provider pursuant to Article 13;
-- src:520 | (e) a description of the implementation of human oversight measures, according to the instructions for use;
-- src:521 | (f) the measures to be taken in the case of the materialisation of those risks, including the arrangements for internal governance and complaint mechanisms.
@ref Art 27(1) (src:515-521)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the facts` IS AN `Art 27(1) who and what`
      `the assessment` IS AN `Art 27(1) the assessment`
      `the assessment was performed prior to deploying the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 27(1) the deployer has performed the assessment of the impact on fundamental rights prior to deploying the system` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF (`Art 27(1) the deployer is required to perform an assessment of the impact on fundamental rights` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` `the facts`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN
            IF       `the assessment was performed prior to deploying the high-risk AI system`
                 AND `the assessment`'s `the assessment contains a description of the deployer's processes in which the high-risk AI system will be used in line with its intended purpose`
                 AND `the assessment`'s `the assessment contains a description of the period of time within which, and the frequency with which, each high-risk AI system is intended to be used`
                 AND `the assessment`'s `the assessment contains the categories of natural persons and groups likely to be affected by its use in the specific context`
                 AND `the assessment`'s `the assessment contains the specific risks of harm likely to have an impact on those categories, taking into account the information given by the provider pursuant to Article 13`
                 AND `the assessment`'s `the assessment contains a description of the implementation of human oversight measures, according to the instructions for use`
                 AND `the assessment`'s `the assessment contains the measures to be taken in the case of the materialisation of those risks, including the arrangements for internal governance and complaint mechanisms`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall perform an assessment of the impact on fundamental rights that the use of such system may produce. For that purpose, deployers shall perform an assessment consisting of: (a) ... (f)"
        ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deployer or the system is outside paragraph 1
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 27, "", 0)

-- "Prior to deploying": the deadline is the date on which the deployer deploys the system, inclusive (fork F-prior-to in NOTES.md).
-- src:515 | 1. Prior to deploying a high-risk AI system referred to in Article 6(2), with the exception of high-risk AI systems intended to be used in the area listed in point 2 of Annex III, deployers that are bodies governed by public law, or are private entities providing public services, and deployers of high-risk AI systems referred to in points 5 (b) and (c) of Annex III, shall perform an assessment of the impact on fundamental rights that the use of such system may produce. For that purpose, deployers shall perform an assessment consisting of:
-- src:516 | (a) a description of the deployer’s processes in which the high-risk AI system will be used in line with its intended purpose;
-- src:517 | (b) a description of the period of time within which, and the frequency with which, each high-risk AI system is intended to be used;
-- src:518 | (c) the categories of natural persons and groups likely to be affected by its use in the specific context;
-- src:519 | (d) the specific risks of harm likely to have an impact on the categories of natural persons or groups of persons identified pursuant to point (c) of this paragraph, taking into account the information given by the provider pursuant to Article 13;
-- src:520 | (e) a description of the implementation of human oversight measures, according to the instructions for use;
-- src:521 | (f) the measures to be taken in the case of the materialisation of those risks, including the arrangements for internal governance and complaint mechanisms.
@ref Art 27(1) (src:515-521)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the facts` IS AN `Art 27(1) who and what`
      `the date on which the deployer deploys the high-risk AI system` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 27 act`
`Art 27(1) the deployer's duty to perform the assessment of the impact on fundamental rights prior to deploying the system` MEANS
    IF       `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
         AND (`Art 27(1) the deployer is required to perform an assessment of the impact on fundamental rights` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` `the facts`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Deployer
         MUST `Art 27(1) perform an assessment of the impact on fundamental rights prior to deploying the high-risk AI system`
         WITHIN daysLeft
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Deployer BECAUSE "no assessment of the impact on fundamental rights was performed prior to deploying the high-risk AI system"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, or the deployer or the system is outside paragraph 1
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 27, "", 0)
        daysLeft MEANS IF (Day `the date on which the deployer deploys the high-risk AI system`) AT LEAST (Day `the date asked`) THEN (Day `the date on which the deployer deploys the high-risk AI system`) MINUS (Day `the date asked`) ELSE 0

§ `Article 27(2): the first use, reliance on earlier assessments, and updating`

-- "The obligation laid down in paragraph 1 applies to the first use of the high-risk AI system": a scope statement with no "only", so a later use is not covered (NOTHING, the periods ruling, rule (c)).
-- src:522 | 2. The obligation laid down in paragraph 1 applies to the first use of the high-risk AI system. The deployer may, in similar cases, rely on previously conducted fundamental rights impact assessments or existing impact assessments carried out by provider. If, during the use of the high-risk AI system, the deployer considers that any of the elements listed in paragraph 1 has changed or is no longer up to date, the deployer shall take the necessary steps to update the information.
@ref Art 27(2) first sentence (src:522)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the use is the first use of the high-risk AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 27(2) the obligation laid down in paragraph 1 applies to the use` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF `the use is the first use of the high-risk AI system`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applies to the first use of the high-risk AI system"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 27, "", 0)

-- "The deployer may, in similar cases, rely on previously conducted fundamental rights impact assessments or existing impact assessments carried out by provider." A grant limited by its own wording: JUST TRUE inside it, NOTHING outside (ruling of 2026-11-12).
-- src:522 | 2. The obligation laid down in paragraph 1 applies to the first use of the high-risk AI system. The deployer may, in similar cases, rely on previously conducted fundamental rights impact assessments or existing impact assessments carried out by provider. If, during the use of the high-risk AI system, the deployer considers that any of the elements listed in paragraph 1 has changed or is no longer up to date, the deployer shall take the necessary steps to update the information.
@ref Art 27(2) second sentence (src:522)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the case is similar to a case in which an assessment was previously conducted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a previously conducted fundamental rights impact assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an existing impact assessment carried out by the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 27(2) the deployer may rely on a previous assessment` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF       `the case is similar to a case in which an assessment was previously conducted`
             AND (`there is a previously conducted fundamental rights impact assessment` OR `there is an existing impact assessment carried out by the provider`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The deployer may, in similar cases, rely on previously conducted fundamental rights impact assessments or existing impact assessments carried out by provider"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 27, "", 0)

-- src:522 | 2. The obligation laid down in paragraph 1 applies to the first use of the high-risk AI system. The deployer may, in similar cases, rely on previously conducted fundamental rights impact assessments or existing impact assessments carried out by provider. If, during the use of the high-risk AI system, the deployer considers that any of the elements listed in paragraph 1 has changed or is no longer up to date, the deployer shall take the necessary steps to update the information.
@ref Art 27(2) third sentence (src:522)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the deployer considers, during the use of the high-risk AI system, that any of the elements listed in paragraph 1 has changed or is no longer up to date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer has taken the necessary steps to update the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 27(2) the deployer has taken the necessary steps to update the information` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the deployer considers, during the use of the high-risk AI system, that any of the elements listed in paragraph 1 has changed or is no longer up to date`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If, during the use of the high-risk AI system, the deployer considers that any of the elements listed in paragraph 1 has changed or is no longer up to date, the deployer shall take the necessary steps to update the information" (the deployer considers no element changed)
        ELSE
             IF `the deployer has taken the necessary steps to update the information`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the deployer shall take the necessary steps to update the information"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 27, "", 0)

@ref Art 27(2) third sentence (src:522)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the deployer considers, during the use of the high-risk AI system, that any of the elements listed in paragraph 1 has changed or is no longer up to date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 27 act`
`Art 27(2) the deployer's duty to take the necessary steps to update the information` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `the deployer considers, during the use of the high-risk AI system, that any of the elements listed in paragraph 1 has changed or is no longer up to date`
    THEN PARTY Deployer
         MUST `Art 27(2) take the necessary steps to update the information`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Deployer BECAUSE "the necessary steps to update the information were not taken"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, or the deployer considers no element changed
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 27, "", 0)


§ `Article 27(3): notifying the market surveillance authority of the results`

-- "Once the assessment ... has been performed, the deployer shall notify the market surveillance authority of its results, submitting the filled-out template ... In the case referred to in Article 46(1), deployers may be exempt from that obligation to notify."
-- No time limit is stated, so no trace reaches a breach. A deployer in the Article 46(1) case that is exempt owes nothing (NOTHING: "may be exempt" is a grant limited by its own wording).
-- src:523 | 3. Once the assessment referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article has been performed, the deployer shall notify the market surveillance authority of its results, submitting the filled-out template referred to in paragraph 5 of this Article as part of the notification. In the case referred to in Article 46(1), deployers may be exempt from that obligation to notify.
@ref Art 27(3) (src:523)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the assessment referred to in paragraph 1 has been performed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer is in the case referred to in Article 46(1) and is exempt from the obligation to notify` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer has notified the market surveillance authority of the results of the assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer has submitted the filled-out template referred to in paragraph 5 as part of the notification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 27(3) the deployer has notified the market surveillance authority of the results` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT `the assessment referred to in paragraph 1 has been performed`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Once the assessment referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article has been performed"
        ELSE IF `the deployer is in the case referred to in Article 46(1) and is exempt from the obligation to notify`
             THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the case referred to in Article 46(1), deployers may be exempt from that obligation to notify"
             ELSE IF `the deployer has notified the market surveillance authority of the results of the assessment` AND `the deployer has submitted the filled-out template referred to in paragraph 5 as part of the notification`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the deployer shall notify the market surveillance authority of its results, submitting the filled-out template referred to in paragraph 5 of this Article as part of the notification"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 27, "", 0)

-- src:523 | 3. Once the assessment referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article has been performed, the deployer shall notify the market surveillance authority of its results, submitting the filled-out template referred to in paragraph 5 of this Article as part of the notification. In the case referred to in Article 46(1), deployers may be exempt from that obligation to notify.
@ref Art 27(3) (src:523)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the assessment referred to in paragraph 1 has been performed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer is in the case referred to in Article 46(1) and is exempt from the obligation to notify` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 27 act`
`Art 27(3) the deployer's duty to notify the market surveillance authority of the results` MEANS
    IF       `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
         AND `the assessment referred to in paragraph 1 has been performed`
         AND NOT `the deployer is in the case referred to in Article 46(1) and is exempt from the obligation to notify`
    THEN PARTY Deployer
         MUST `Art 27(3) notify the market surveillance authority of the results of the assessment, submitting the filled-out template`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Deployer BECAUSE "the market surveillance authority was not notified of the results of the assessment with the filled-out template"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, the assessment has not been performed, or the deployer is exempt
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 27, "", 0)

§ `Article 27(4): the data protection impact assessment (replaced by the Omnibus: as enacted and as amended)`

-- VERSION as enacted (base line 1056): "If any of the obligations laid down in this Article is already met through the data protection impact assessment ..., the fundamental rights impact assessment referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article shall complement that data protection impact assessment."
-- A duty: JUST TRUE when the fundamental rights impact assessment complements the data protection impact assessment, JUST FALSE when it does not, NOTHING where no obligation is already met through the data protection impact assessment.
-- No date and no gate: the dispatcher below never reaches it (Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply only after 27 July 2026), so the text as enacted is tested through this function.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1056 | 4. If any of the obligations laid down in this Article is already met through the data protection impact assessment conducted pursuant to Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Article 27 of Directive (EU) 2016/680, the fundamental rights impact assessment referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article shall complement that data protection impact assessment.
@ref Art 27(4) as enacted (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1056)
GIVEN `an obligation laid down in this Article is already met through the data protection impact assessment conducted pursuant to Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Article 27 of Directive (EU) 2016/680` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fundamental rights impact assessment referred to in paragraph 1 complements that data protection impact assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 27(4) as enacted the assessment complies with paragraph 4` MEANS
    IF NOT `an obligation laid down in this Article is already met through the data protection impact assessment conducted pursuant to Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Article 27 of Directive (EU) 2016/680`
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If any of the obligations laid down in this Article is already met through the data protection impact assessment"
    ELSE IF `the fundamental rights impact assessment referred to in paragraph 1 complements that data protection impact assessment`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the fundamental rights impact assessment referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article shall complement that data protection impact assessment"

-- VERSION as amended (consolidated line 525): the duty to complement is replaced by a permission: "the deployer may, when conducting the fundamental rights impact assessment referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, include cross-references to the relevant sections of that data protection impact assessment or include relevant parts thereof".
-- A grant gated by "If" and "when conducting": JUST TRUE when both hold, NOTHING when either fails (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12; fork F-27-4-meaning in NOTES.md).
-- src:525 | 4. If any of the obligations laid down in this Article is already met through the data protection impact assessment conducted pursuant to Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Article 27 of Directive (EU) 2016/680, the deployer may, when conducting the fundamental rights impact assessment referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, include cross-references to the relevant sections of that data protection impact assessment or include relevant parts thereof in the fundamental rights impact assessment.
@ref Art 27(4) as amended (src:525)
GIVEN `an obligation laid down in this Article is already met through the data protection impact assessment conducted pursuant to Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Article 27 of Directive (EU) 2016/680` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer is conducting the fundamental rights impact assessment referred to in paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 27(4) as amended the deployer may include cross-references to the data protection impact assessment or relevant parts of it` MEANS
    IF `an obligation laid down in this Article is already met through the data protection impact assessment conducted pursuant to Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Article 27 of Directive (EU) 2016/680` AND `the deployer is conducting the fundamental rights impact assessment referred to in paragraph 1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If any of the obligations laid down in this Article is already met through the data protection impact assessment ..., the deployer may, when conducting the fundamental rights impact assessment referred to in paragraph 1"

-- The dispatcher, on the date asked: whether the deployer's assessment stands as paragraph 4 of the text in force provides. As enacted that is the duty to complement; as amended it is the permission to cross-refer.
-- src:525 | 4. If any of the obligations laid down in this Article is already met through the data protection impact assessment conducted pursuant to Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Article 27 of Directive (EU) 2016/680, the deployer may, when conducting the fundamental rights impact assessment referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, include cross-references to the relevant sections of that data protection impact assessment or include relevant parts thereof in the fundamental rights impact assessment.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1056 | 4. If any of the obligations laid down in this Article is already met through the data protection impact assessment conducted pursuant to Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Article 27 of Directive (EU) 2016/680, the fundamental rights impact assessment referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article shall complement that data protection impact assessment.
@ref Art 27(4) (src:525) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1056)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `an obligation laid down in this Article is already met through the data protection impact assessment conducted pursuant to Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Article 27 of Directive (EU) 2016/680` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deployer is conducting the fundamental rights impact assessment referred to in paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fundamental rights impact assessment referred to in paragraph 1 complements that data protection impact assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 27(4) the assessment stands as paragraph 4 provides` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
        WHEN `as enacted` THEN                                                                  -- VERSION as enacted
            `Art 27(4) as enacted the assessment complies with paragraph 4` `an obligation laid down in this Article is already met through the data protection impact assessment conducted pursuant to Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Article 27 of Directive (EU) 2016/680` `the fundamental rights impact assessment referred to in paragraph 1 complements that data protection impact assessment`
        WHEN `as amended` THEN                                                                  -- VERSION as amended
            `Art 27(4) as amended the deployer may include cross-references to the data protection impact assessment or relevant parts of it` `an obligation laid down in this Article is already met through the data protection impact assessment conducted pursuant to Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Article 27 of Directive (EU) 2016/680` `the deployer is conducting the fundamental rights impact assessment referred to in paragraph 1`
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 27, "", 0)

-- The regulative rule: as enacted a MUST (complement), as amended a MAY (cross-refer, with no LEST: a permission unused is no breach). No time limit is stated.
-- src:525 | 4. If any of the obligations laid down in this Article is already met through the data protection impact assessment conducted pursuant to Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Article 27 of Directive (EU) 2016/680, the deployer may, when conducting the fundamental rights impact assessment referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article, include cross-references to the relevant sections of that data protection impact assessment or include relevant parts thereof in the fundamental rights impact assessment.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1056 | 4. If any of the obligations laid down in this Article is already met through the data protection impact assessment conducted pursuant to Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Article 27 of Directive (EU) 2016/680, the fundamental rights impact assessment referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article shall complement that data protection impact assessment.
@ref Art 27(4) (src:525) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1056)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `an obligation laid down in this Article is already met through the data protection impact assessment conducted pursuant to Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Article 27 of Directive (EU) 2016/680` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 27 act`
`Art 27(4) the deployer's duty or permission concerning the data protection impact assessment` MEANS
    IF       `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
         AND `an obligation laid down in this Article is already met through the data protection impact assessment conducted pursuant to Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Article 27 of Directive (EU) 2016/680`
    THEN CONSIDER `Omnibus Art 4 the version in force` `the date asked`
         WHEN `as enacted` THEN                                                                  -- VERSION as enacted
             PARTY Deployer
             MUST `Art 27(4) as enacted complement the data protection impact assessment`
             HENCE FULFILLED
             LEST BREACH BY Deployer BECAUSE "the fundamental rights impact assessment did not complement the data protection impact assessment"
         WHEN `as amended` THEN                                                                  -- VERSION as amended
             PARTY Deployer
             MAY `Art 27(4) as amended include cross-references to the data protection impact assessment or include relevant parts of it in the fundamental rights impact assessment`
             HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, or no obligation of this Article is already met through the data protection impact assessment
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 27, "", 0)

§ `Article 27(5): the AI Office's template for a questionnaire (replaced by the Omnibus: as enacted and as amended; addressed to an official, no seat)`

-- "The AI Office shall develop a template for a questionnaire, including through an automated tool, to facilitate deployers in complying with their obligations under this Article in a simplified manner."
-- It matters to a deployer because paragraph 3 asks it to submit the filled-out template: the function says whether the template exists as the paragraph describes it. VERSION as enacted has the first sentence only.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1057 | 5. The AI Office shall develop a template for a questionnaire, including through an automated tool, to facilitate deployers in complying with their obligations under this Article in a simplified manner.
@ref Art 27(5) as enacted (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1057)
GIVEN `the AI Office has developed a template for a questionnaire, including through an automated tool, to facilitate deployers in complying with their obligations under this Article in a simplified manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 27(5) as enacted the AI Office has developed the template` MEANS
    `the AI Office has developed a template for a questionnaire, including through an automated tool, to facilitate deployers in complying with their obligations under this Article in a simplified manner`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The AI Office shall develop a template for a questionnaire, including through an automated tool, to facilitate deployers in complying with their obligations under this Article in a simplified manner"

-- VERSION as amended: the Omnibus adds "This template shall, where relevant, give deployers the possibility to include cross-references to the relevant sections of the data protection impact assessment or include relevant parts thereof in the fundamental rights impact assessment pursuant to paragraph 4."
-- "where relevant" is a limit in the text's own wording: a template for which it is not relevant needs no such possibility.
-- src:526 | 5. The AI Office shall develop a template for a questionnaire, including through an automated tool, to facilitate deployers in complying with their obligations under this Article in a simplified manner. This template shall, where relevant, give deployers the possibility to include cross-references to the relevant sections of the data protection impact assessment or include relevant parts thereof in the fundamental rights impact assessment pursuant to paragraph 4.
@ref Art 27(5) as amended (src:526)
GIVEN `the AI Office has developed a template for a questionnaire, including through an automated tool, to facilitate deployers in complying with their obligations under this Article in a simplified manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `giving deployers the possibility to cross-refer to the data protection impact assessment is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the template gives deployers the possibility to include cross-references to the relevant sections of the data protection impact assessment or include relevant parts thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 27(5) as amended the AI Office has developed the template` MEANS
        `the AI Office has developed a template for a questionnaire, including through an automated tool, to facilitate deployers in complying with their obligations under this Article in a simplified manner`
    AND ((NOT `giving deployers the possibility to cross-refer to the data protection impact assessment is relevant`) OR `the template gives deployers the possibility to include cross-references to the relevant sections of the data protection impact assessment or include relevant parts thereof`)
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The AI Office shall develop a template for a questionnaire ... This template shall, where relevant, give deployers the possibility to include cross-references to the relevant sections of the data protection impact assessment or include relevant parts thereof in the fundamental rights impact assessment pursuant to paragraph 4"

-- src:526 | 5. The AI Office shall develop a template for a questionnaire, including through an automated tool, to facilitate deployers in complying with their obligations under this Article in a simplified manner. This template shall, where relevant, give deployers the possibility to include cross-references to the relevant sections of the data protection impact assessment or include relevant parts thereof in the fundamental rights impact assessment pursuant to paragraph 4.
-- src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1057 | 5. The AI Office shall develop a template for a questionnaire, including through an automated tool, to facilitate deployers in complying with their obligations under this Article in a simplified manner.
@ref Art 27(5) (src:526) (src:eu-ai-act-2024-1689:1057)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the AI Office has developed a template for a questionnaire, including through an automated tool, to facilitate deployers in complying with their obligations under this Article in a simplified manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `giving deployers the possibility to cross-refer to the data protection impact assessment is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the template gives deployers the possibility to include cross-references to the relevant sections of the data protection impact assessment or include relevant parts thereof` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 27(5) the AI Office has developed the template` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
